     "result_text_tail": "alculated ones are our estimates, each with its formula on the slide and as a live formula in the workbook. No \"?\" placeholders are left. The step that re-checks sources against the web didn't apply, because the only source is the briefing pack.\n\n**Choices I made for you:**\n- **Audience:** the CEO and executive team deciding at January 2027 planning.\n- **Theme:** navy, the skill's default.\n- **Storyline:** built as I planned it, with no review step.\n\n**Assumptions to know about:**\n- **Pro uptake of 33%** carries most of the case. At the paywall's 14% rate, Pro adds only about $1.2M a year.\n- **Pro's AI cost assumes usage scales with seats.** That gives about $4 of each $12 seat. Beta accounts were more active than the base, so this probably overstates the cost.\n- **The $1.1M mobile delay cost is an upper bound.** It assumes the rewrite would stop all mobile-driven churn the day it ships.\n- **The 13-month payback** is recorded in the workbook as a plain calculation rather than an estimate, though it depends on the Pro profit estimate. Its formula note says so.\n\nNext, I could switch the theme, add a page showing results at different Pro uptake levels, or tighten any slide you want to change.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- brightwork-dispatch-copilot.pptx\n- brightwork-dispatch-copilot-sources.xlsx\n- brightwork-dispatch-copilot.json (the spec the deck is rendered from)\n- NOTES.md (the choices and assumptions above)\n\nThe script that generates the spec is `./work/build_spec.py`."
    }
